      ...
    }
  }
}
```

Previously, fixed schedule inference load mode was supported via `--schedule` option (e.g. `--schedule=2,4`, timestamps in seconds).

Now, that option is removed and timestamps are pulled from the input data JSON (timestamps in milliseconds), which might look like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "payload": [
        {
          "model": "facebook/opt-125m",
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "What is the capital of France?"
            }
          ],
          "max_tokens": 8
        }
      ],
      "timestamp": [
        2000
      ]
    },
    {
      "payload": [
        {
          "model": "facebook/opt-125m",
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "What is 2+2?"
            }
          ],
          "max_tokens": 8
        }
      ],
      "timestamp": [
        4000
      ]
    },
  ]
}
```
